0..65 Comment "// The family a code defines, and its decoder, with each refusal."
66..68 Comment "//"
69..143 Comment "// The family holds the arguments its code asks for. Those arguments range"
144..218 Comment "// over the family itself. The decoder decodes the arguments. It reads the"
219..293 Comment "// family\'s elements through itself. The codes exist for these two things."
294..296 Comment "//"
297..374 Comment "// A call computes the type of the arguments. The family thus occurs inside a"
375..450 Comment "// call in its own field. The occurrence walk refuses it. The decoder calls"
451..527 Comment "// itself through `decodeArgs`. That call stands at no stage below the code."
528..607 Comment "// The marked call in `decodeArgs` stages the code, and the code\'s case refines"
608..686 Comment "// the arguments\' type. The arguments\' second field then reads as unknown. The"
687..743 Comment "// checker unfolds `args` and loses its own marked call."
744..746 Comment "//"
747..827 Comment "// - see: #3575 — not implemented: the family a code defines, with its decoder"
828..910 Comment "// - see: #3733 — a decoder\'s unfolded body reads its own marked call as unknown"
911..987 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the codes and their arguments,"
988..1001 Comment "//   admitted"
1003..1019 Comment "// The naturals."
